course: dictionary
lesson: 8434
title: What is a sacrament?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sacrament is a special ceremony in a Christian church. You can often spot the context clues: «A sacrament is a church ceremony Christians believe is an outward sign of God's grace.» So a sacrament is a church ceremony, and it is linked to God.
explain: Grace means God's love and help given to people. An outward sign is something you can see, hear or touch. Christians use ordinary things such as water, bread and wine, so the word sacrament points to something ordinary that shows something holy.
explain: Look for clues in the next sentence: «Catholics celebrate Mass and have seven sacraments.» The sentence tells you that churches count sacraments, like a list you can number. When you meet a new word, ask what would fit in its place, then check the meaning in the sentence.
fact: A sacrament is a holy ceremony in Christian churches.
fact: Christians believe a sacrament is an outward sign of God's grace, which means God's love and help.
fact: Catholic and Orthodox churches count seven sacraments: baptism, confirmation, Eucharist, confession, anointing of the sick, marriage and holy orders.
fact: Most Protestant churches count two sacraments: baptism and the Lord's Supper.
fact: Quakers and the Salvation Army do not hold outward sacraments.
exercise: «A sacrament is a church ceremony Christians believe is an outward sign of God's grace.» What is God's grace? | A special hymn | *God's love and help given to people | A church building | Money given to the church
exercise: Catholic and Orthodox churches count how many sacraments? | Five | Ten | Two | *Seven
exercise: Which of these is one of the sacraments named in the lessons? | *Baptism | Singing | Reading the newspaper | Painting a picture
test: Most Protestant churches count how many sacraments? | Seven | Five | Twelve | *Two
test: Which two sacraments do most Protestant churches count? | Baptism and marriage | *Baptism and the Lord's Supper | Anointing of the sick and holy orders | Confession and confirmation
exam: Which group does not hold outward sacraments? | Most Protestant churches | Catholics | Orthodox churches | *Quakers
